\textbf{Solution:} Let's substitute $A(-4,0)$, $C(2,6)$ into $y=\frac{1}{2}x^{2}+bx+c$, we get: $\left\{\begin{array}{l}0=\frac{1}{2}\times 16-4b+c \\ 6=\frac{1}{2}\times 4+2b+c\end{array}\right.$. Solving these, we find $\left\{\begin{array}{l}b=2 \\ c=0\end{array}\right.$, \\
$\therefore$ the equation of the parabola is $y=\frac{1}{2}x^{2}+2x=\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{2}-2$, \\
$\therefore$ the coordinates of the vertex $M$ are $\boxed{(-2，-2)}$;
